Statement of modification
-------------------------

The Holistic Universe Model simulator began from the Tychosium source as a
starting point and has been substantially modified since.

What derives from the upstream work is the settings-object schema (field names
such as containerObj, orbitCentera/b/c, orbitTilta/b, pivotObj, planetObj,
startPos) together with the generic routine that walks that array to compose
nested Three.js Object3D containers, plus assorted rendering and utility
helpers. That is an engine interface, not a model.

The scene graph itself is original. The Tychosium builds 31 nodes on an
epicycle/deferent geometry; this project builds 73 nodes on a precession
hierarchy.

Also original: the Expanding Solar System Resonance Theory, the six Fibonacci
Laws, the L1 climate formula, the planet inspector, the LOD-climate tool, the
Earth Fundamental Cycle (H) lattice, the deep-time engine, the derived moon, the
fitting pipeline, the verification suite and the documentation. The upstream
work is 3,432 lines; this one is 64,673.

The Tychosium implements the TYCHOS model of Simon Shack. This project implements
a different model and reaches different conclusions; the shared lineage is in the
simulation scaffolding, not in the astronomy.

